st identifiers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to prose names, with byte-identical CLI, JSON, help, and docs output.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob prose with permanent legacy aliases[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine-rename[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-cli: one predicate reads both type spellings, writers emit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][\\[prose]], bob prose becomes canonical with bob articles as a hidden [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]alias, copy and docs move to prose, and a section-numbers flag plus a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]host probe ship; wire vocabulary stays frozen.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Prose in Obsidian[/bold #D7AFFF]                                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-plugins[dim] · [dim][/dim]after prose-cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-plugins: four plugins detect both spellings, display names and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command titles change under unchanged ids, a Toggle section numbers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command lands, plugin docs are fixed, and the bundles deploy with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]currency marker.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Host gate, vault cutover, and canonical plugin calls[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]prose-vault[dim] · [dim][/dim]after prose-cli, prose-plugins[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prose-vault: pass the host-currency gate, retype the one live note and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rename the vault's type files, switch plugin calls to bob prose, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]apply only accepted memory decisions.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plan prose-section extract and inline[/bold #D7AFFF]             